+# Daily Grind
+
+Run `npm start` to serve the homepage and newsletter endpoint with Node.js 22 or newer.
+The port defaults to `11222`; set `PORT` to override it. No dependencies or build step are required.
+
+Newsletter submissions are appended to `data/newsletter.jsonl` on this server.
+Set `NEWSLETTER_FILE` to choose another location, and use a persistent volume when deploying.
+This stores the signup list; it does not send newsletter campaigns.
+Only the homepage, stylesheet, and client script are publicly served.
+
+The Node server applies Content Security Policy headers to every response. Scripts,
+styles, requests, and form submissions are restricted to this origin; images may
+also load from `https://images.unsplash.com`. Inline scripts, inline styles,
+embedded objects, framing, and changes to the document base URL are blocked.
+The form reports network/HTTP failures and enforced policy violations to customers.
+
+Run `npm test` for automated handler and client checks. These use mocked requests
+and DOM elements and do not listen on a port or launch a browser.
